[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124633,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lymphoepithelial carcinoma is a poorly differentiated squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) admixed with variable amounts of lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124634,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8082/3 Lymphoepithelial carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124635,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C31.Z &amp; XH1E40 Cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma &amp; Lymphoepithelial carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124636,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> lymphoepithelioma-like carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124637,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124638,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lymphoepithelial carcinoma of the skin typically involves sun-exposed skin, most often of the head and neck.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124639,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This rare type of SCC typically shows rapid growth, but it has no features to distinguish it from other SCC types.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124640,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lymphoepithelial carcinomas of the skin are exceedingly rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124641,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is similar to that of common forms of SCC (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/64/35\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Squamous cell carcinomas</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124642,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although lymphoepithelial carcinoma of the skin resembles undifferentiated nasopharyngeal carcinoma (lymphoepithelioma) histologically, a strong association with EBV has not been demonstrated {29723365}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124643,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/64/35\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Squamous cell carcinomas</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124644,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Lymphoepithelial carcinoma of the skin is characterized by poorly differentiated tumour cell islands surrounded and infiltrated by lymphocytes and variable numbers of plasma cells {25102913}. Accordingly, the lesions resemble undifferentiated nasopharyngeal carcinoma. Immunohistochemistry (pancytokeratin, CK5/6, or p63) confirms the presence of epithelial elements that may be masked by the lymphoid component.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Lymphoepithelial carcinoma of the skin must be distinguished from reactive and neoplastic lymphoid infiltrates of the skin, or inflamed SCC {25102913}. Lymphadenoma has a banal epithelial component {11763398}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:56:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124645,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124646,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124647,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a poorly differentiated SCC; tumour islands surrounded and infiltrated by lymphocytes and variable numbers of plasma cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124648,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours should be staged according to the eighth edition of the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM system.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124649,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 398,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Excision is usually sufficient, but radiotherapy is sometimes used in cases with positive margins {23133769; 31501980}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T14:55:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]